1
00:00:00,033 --> 00:00:01,633
In the digital asset space

2
00:00:01,700 --> 00:00:05,666
One flaw in a smart contract can wipe out tens of millions of dollars

3
00:00:06,033 --> 00:00:06,533
Today

4
00:00:06,533 --> 00:00:09,233
investors lean on AI to audit contracts

5
00:00:09,233 --> 00:00:10,600
read on-chain data

6
00:00:10,600 --> 00:00:12,333
and run DeFi strategies

7
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:15,666
But do these models really understand digital assets?

8
00:00:15,900 --> 00:00:17,833
Introducing DMind Benchmark

9
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:21,666
The first test of how well AI understands digital assets

10
00:00:21,666 --> 00:00:23,433
covering nine core areas:

11
00:00:23,433 --> 00:00:24,533
blockchain basics

12
00:00:24,533 --> 00:00:26,300
smart contracts, tokenomics

13
00:00:26,300 --> 00:00:27,200
memecoins

14
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:28,733
security, and more

15
00:00:28,833 --> 00:00:33,266
We pulled 6.1 gigabytes of data from 39 trusted sources

16
00:00:33,533 --> 00:00:34,533
Five experts

17
00:00:34,533 --> 00:00:36,233
each with eight years in the field

18
00:00:36,233 --> 00:00:39,833
turned it into 3,543 questions

19
00:00:39,833 --> 00:00:42,666
Every question is traceable and checked for leaks

20
00:00:42,666 --> 00:00:46,433
so a model cannot memorize the answers and game its score

21
00:00:46,433 --> 00:00:47,000
First

22
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:49,666
we tested 31 of the top AI models

23
00:00:49,666 --> 00:00:51,133
They handle the basics well

24
00:00:51,133 --> 00:00:53,233
but all fall down on the harder problems

25
00:00:53,233 --> 00:00:56,066
like tokenomics and spotting security flaws

26
00:00:56,066 --> 00:01:00,700
Even the strongest model could not break 80 out of 100 in the security area

27
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:01,900
In the real world

28
00:01:01,900 --> 00:01:03,533
AI rarely works alone

29
00:01:03,633 --> 00:01:04,700
It runs as an agent

30
00:01:04,700 --> 00:01:05,800
calling tools

31
00:01:05,800 --> 00:01:08,033
So we tested five AI agents

32
00:01:08,033 --> 00:01:09,900
each with three real skills:

33
00:01:09,900 --> 00:01:11,100
blockchain development

34
00:01:11,100 --> 00:01:12,133
contract security

35
00:01:12,133 --> 00:01:13,533
and tokenomics

36
00:01:13,666 --> 00:01:15,666
But no agent ran away with it

37
00:01:15,733 --> 00:01:17,900
The five finished nearly seven points apart

38
00:01:17,900 --> 00:01:21,300
and tokenomics and security stayed their weakest spots

39
00:01:21,433 --> 00:01:24,000
DMind handles agents on real tasks too

40
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:26,266
and it still tells the strong from the weak

41
00:01:26,266 --> 00:01:28,733
Could the models just be memorizing the test?

42
00:01:28,900 --> 00:01:30,900
We trained them directly on the questions

43
00:01:30,900 --> 00:01:32,933
and the scores barely moved

44
00:01:32,933 --> 00:01:35,433
You cannot fake this benchmark by cramming

45
00:01:35,433 --> 00:01:37,133
It rewards real reasoning

46
00:01:37,266 --> 00:01:40,200
Since we open-sourced it in April 2025

47
00:01:40,300 --> 00:01:43,800
DMind has hit number one on Hugging Face's trending list

48
00:01:43,800 --> 00:01:46,266
with over 13,000 downloads

49
00:01:46,266 --> 00:01:50,000
The full dataset and testing tools are free for anyone to use

50
00:01:50,233 --> 00:01:51,800
DMind Benchmark

51
00:01:51,866 --> 00:01:55,300
Now you can finally see whether AI can be trusted with your money

